# Learned rules

Scan this table before acting. Use a row when its **Scope** matches the task (or scope is `agent`).

Hard rules in `docs/PRODUCT.md` and `.cursor/rules/scoresense-core.mdc` beat this table.

## How to apply frequency

| Freq | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `always` | Do this whenever the condition is true. No silent skip. |
| `never` | Do not do this. No silent exception. |
| `usually` | Default. If you deviate, say why in the reply. |
| `rarely` | Do not do this unless the user asked this turn or a hard rule requires it. |

## Catalog

Keep under 30 data rows. Promote `always` / `never` into `docs/PRODUCT.md` or a domain `.mdc` and delete the row. Do not invent rows here except via `.cursor/skills/capture-correction/SKILL.md`. Do not restate a hard rule from `docs/PRODUCT.md`, a registry `doNot`, or a skill.

| Freq | Scope | Rule |
|------|-------|------|
| usually | agent | For a redesign or new page, write 2-3 static HTML mock options in docs/mockups, then implement the pick. Mock pages must pass `layout_audit` too. Include a screenshot of each option so the user can pick visually. Skip design essays on the mock pass. |
| usually | agent | Address review comments on the existing PR branch. Do not open a new branch for the same review. |
| usually | agent | When the user says ready to merge, rebase onto develop, address review, and mark the PR ready. |
| usually | projections | When GBM weekly is missing for K or DEF, fill the week from the rank-curve per-game number. |
| never | agent | Do not demote the second .btn-primary in DOM order to satisfy the layout audit; primaries are a judgment list the user approves. |
